<!------------------------------------------------ MONGODB_SESSION_ARCHITECTURE ------------------------------------------------>

<div class="container my-5">

  <div class="card shadow-lg border-0 rounded-4">

    <!-- Header -->

    <div class="card-header bg-success text-white p-4">

      <h2 class="fw-bold mb-1">

        🗄️ MongoDB + Express Session Architecture

      </h2>

      <p class="mb-0">

        Understand how MongoDB, Express Server and Express Session work together.

      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- Body -->

    <div class="card-body">

      <div class="alert alert-info">

        During login, Express first verifies the user from MongoDB.
        After successful verification, Express Session stores the
        user's login information on the server and sends only the
        Session ID to the browser.

      </div>

      <pre class="bg-dark text-light rounded p-4">

                USER

                 │

                 ▼

        Open Login Page

                 │

                 ▼

        Enter Email & Password

                 │

                 ▼

          POST /login

                 │

                 ▼

        Express Controller

                 │

                 ▼

     Search User In MongoDB

                 │

        User.findOne()

                 │

      ┌──────────┴──────────┐

      │                     │

      ▼                     ▼

 User Not Found       User Found

      │                     │

      ▼                     ▼

 Login Failed      Verify Password

                            │

                            ▼

                  Create Session

                            │

                            ▼

req.session.user={

    id,

    username,

    email,

    role

}

                            │

                            ▼

Server Stores Session

                            │

                            ▼

Browser Receives Cookie

connect.sid

                            │

                            ▼

User Opens Dashboard

                            │

                            ▼

Browser Sends connect.sid

                            │

                            ▼

Express Session

                            │

                            ▼

Find Session

                            │

                            ▼

Dashboard Loaded

</pre>

      <hr>

      <h3>

        📊 Complete Authentication Process

      </h3>

      <table class="table table-bordered">

        <thead class="table-dark">

          <tr>

            <th width="12%">

              Step

            </th>

            <th>

              Process

            </th>

          </tr>

        </thead>

        <tbody>

          <tr>

            <td>1</td>

            <td>

              User enters Email and Password.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>2</td>

            <td>

              Express receives POST /login request.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>3</td>

            <td>

              Mongoose searches the user inside MongoDB.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>4</td>

            <td>

              Password is verified.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>5</td>

            <td>

              Express Session creates req.session.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>6</td>

            <td>

              User information is stored in req.session.user.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>7</td>

            <td>

              Browser receives connect.sid cookie.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>8</td>

            <td>

              Every future request automatically sends connect.sid.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>9</td>

            <td>

              Express finds the Session and allows access to protected pages.

            </td>

          </tr>

          <tr>

            <td>10</td>

            <td>

              Logout destroys the Session and user authentication ends.

            </td>

          </tr>

        </tbody>

      </table>

      <hr>

      <div class="alert alert-success">

        <h5>

          💡 Remember

        </h5>

        <ul class="mb-0">

          <li>

            MongoDB stores permanent user records.

          </li>

          <li>

            Express Session stores temporary login information.

          </li>

          <li>

            Browser stores only the <strong>connect.sid</strong> cookie.

          </li>

          <li>

            Server stores the complete <strong>req.session</strong> object.

          </li>

          <li>

            When the Session expires, the user must log in again.

          </li>

        </ul>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</div>